/*
:name: unbounded_out_cone
:type: equiv
*/
// The tree aegraph (upass/aeg) keeps the cone of an output with no declared width exactly as written: tolg gives
// such a port its driver's width and sign, so folding `(a + b + 1) - 1` to the `a + b` already computed, or a
// quotient plus zero to the quotient, would change the port and could pick a spelling whose width does not hold
// the value (S8 + U8 is 382; U8 / -1 is -255). A `mod`, since the step rewrites only a body tolg alone reads. The
// divisor is odd, so never zero (cgen's `/` by zero is X to the yosys oracle).
pub mod top(a:S8, b:U8, c:U8, d:S8) -> (o:Signed@[0], p:Signed@[0], q:Signed@[0], r:Signed@[0], s:Signed@[0], t:Signed@[0]) {
  o = (a + b + 1) - 1
  p = (c + a) - 0
  q = a - (0 - c)
  r = (b / (d | 1)) + 0
  s = a + b
  t = b / (d | 1)
}
